  "result": "Perfect! All 101 tests pass. The VAT implementation is complete. Here's what was added:\n\n## Summary of VAT Implementation\n\n### 1. **VAT Calculation** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- VAT is calculated per line on the amount **after discount**\n- Formula: `lineVat = Math.round((lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100)`\n- VAT is rounded per line using `Math.round()`\n- Total VAT is the sum of all rounded line VATs\n\n### 2. **Updated invoiceTotals** \nReturns: `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- `subtotal` = sum of all line totals\n- `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n- `vat` = sum of all line VATs (rounded per line)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat\n- All amounts clamped to 0 minimum\n\n### 3. **Updated renderInvoiceText** (`src/render.js`)\nShows:\n- Line items\n- Subtotal (if > 0)\n- Discount (if > 0, shown with minus sign)\n- VAT (if > 0)\n- Total (always shown)\n\n### 4. **Comprehensive Tests** (101 total)\n- VAT calculation with different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- VAT calculated on discounted amounts\n- VAT rounded per line\n- Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n- Combined discount and VAT\n- Render output shows VAT line above total\n\nAll existing tests were updated to account for VAT in totals, and the new functionality is fully tested.",
